From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jacky <me@jackyu.cn>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 09:14:21 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] Walk the DART on t8110 only

Addresses that arrive over the mailbox are translated through dart-sep's
stream zero, whose registers are read at 0x2_5D2C_0000, the t8110 DART.
Virtualization.framework (vresearch1) maps nothing there for a guest with
less than about 7.5 GiB of memory. With only the warm-boot fix, a 6144 MB
guest entered restore mode and lost restored right after NORData ("Could not
read data (-256)") with no crash report from the framework; with this change
the same restore finishes, and the guest then boots with its SEP on this ROM
and comes back from a reboot. With more memory the read is guest RAM, which
only works while that RAM still reads zero.

The platform row gains walks_dart; vresearch1 uses the address as it is,
which is what those reads amounted to on the 8 GiB guests the platform was
validated on. t8110 is unchanged.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
